<https://w3id.org/optimar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n    Version 2.4 (2026-10-16) - Review-driven fixes, alignments and competency-question coverage:\n    - The ontology IRI is now https://w3id.org/optimar (no '#'); the namespace remains https://w3id.org/optimar#\n    - Fixed the SOSA namespace (http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/)\n    - Metadata now uses valid DCMI/BIBO terms (dc:name and dcterms:status removed)\n    - Explicit alignment with SOSA and PROV-O (madeBySensor, isInstalledIn/hasInstalled, Component, Data, Actor, Task, Event)\n    - Declared the Base class (used but undeclared since v2.0) and fixed the failure disjointness axioms\n    - New modules: floating substructure members, mooring system components and classification, anchors and seabed\n    - New sensor properties (sampling frequency, data format) and mechanical properties (stiffness, elastic modulus, inertia, draft)\n    - Maintenance-failure relations (addressesFailure, triggeredBy) to trace the observation -> event -> failure -> maintenance chain\n    - operationalStatus deprecated in favour of hasOperationalState\n    - houses, isHousedIn and precededBy declared transitive; domain and range for monitors, monitoredBy and hasGeneratedData\n    "@en .
<https://w3id.org/optimar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "\n    Versión 2.4 (2026-10-16) - Correcciones derivadas de la revisión, alineamientos y cobertura de las preguntas de competencia:\n    - La IRI de la ontología pasa a ser https://w3id.org/optimar (sin '#'); el espacio de nombres sigue siendo https://w3id.org/optimar#\n    - Corregido el espacio de nombres de SOSA (http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/)\n    - Metadatos con términos válidos de DCMI/BIBO (se eliminan dc:name y dcterms:status)\n    - Alineamiento explícito con SOSA y PROV-O (madeBySensor, isInstalledIn/hasInstalled, Component, Data, Actor, Task, Event)\n    - Declarada la clase Base (usada pero no declarada desde la v2.0) y corregidos los axiomas de disyunción de fallos\n    - Nuevos módulos: miembros de la subestructura flotante, componentes y clasificación del sistema de amarre, anclas y fondo marino\n    - Nuevas propiedades de sensores (frecuencia de muestreo, formato de datos) y mecánicas (rigidez, módulo elástico, inercia, calado)\n    - Relaciones mantenimiento-fallo (addressesFailure, triggeredBy) para trazar la cadena observación -> evento -> fallo -> mantenimiento\n    - operationalStatus queda obsoleta en favor de hasOperationalState\n    - houses, isHousedIn y precededBy pasan a ser transitivas; dominio y rango para monitors, monitoredBy y hasGeneratedData\n    "@es .
<https://w3id.org/optimar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://github.com/bisite/OPTIMAR-Ontology> .
